From f30a9ec1768059d65c06506a01349afefca39153 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dario Gabriel Lipicar <dario@status.im>
Date: Thu, 26 Nov 2026 18:05:16 -0300
Subject: [PATCH 4/5] feat(sync): fetch matched blocks in the background

UpdateSubscriber::fetch_blocks_with takes a function that fetches a
matched block by other means than the node's peers (a Tor errand, in the
wallet core). Each block's fetch starts as its filter matches, while the
scan goes on, so a slow fetch never holds the filters back.

Fetched blocks are applied oldest first, up to the first still under
way, and the scripts they reveal are watched from then on. synced() is
false while any fetch is pending, and at the tip, each fetch that lets
blocks apply makes an update. The fetcher answers None for a block no
longer in the chain, which is skipped. Without a fetcher, matched blocks
are fetched and applied in turn, as upstream does.
